# UST.G3CB B69-B103 H20 Frame Intertwiner

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_GOOD_REDUCTION_FRAME_ISOMORPHISM_AND_CHARACTERISTIC_ZERO_INVERTIBILITY_VALUES_OPEN`

## Theorem

The frozen B69 spectral trace-test frame and the B103 H20 residue frame each
contain 248 ordered monomial classes, but they are not the same ordered list.
Direct comparison gives

```text
shared monomials: 215
B69-only monomials: 33
B103-only monomials: 33.
```

At the common good-reduction fiber `(11,gamma-3)`, reduce all 248 B69
primitive rows through the frozen original-Jacobian H20 coordinate solver.
The resulting matrix `M` has columns equal to the B69 rows expressed in the
B103 H20 basis. The full 282-row ambient reconstruction has zero residual,
and all 215 shared monomials give the expected identity columns.

Exact elimination over `GF(11)` gives

```text
shape(M) = 248 x 248,
rank(M) = 248,
det(M) = 5 mod 11.
```

The emitted inverse satisfies both `M M^{-1}=I` and `M^{-1} M=I`. Because the
determinant is a unit at the common good-reduction place, the two lifted row
sets are bases of the same rank-248 H20 module over the local DVR and hence
over `Q(gamma)`.

## Consequence

The former row-order ambiguity is closed without relabeling either frame. If
`b` is a covector evaluated on the B103 H20 basis and `c` is the same covector
evaluated on the B69 spectral rows, then

```text
c = M^T b,
b = M^{-T} c.
```

Thus any selected source whose 248 B69 trace values are known can be moved
exactly into the B103 H20-dual frame at the good fiber.

## Boundary

The theorem emits the matrix entries only modulo 11. It proves generic
characteristic-zero invertibility, but does not reconstruct the
characteristic-zero matrix entries, identify the terminal G3BI and B89
fibers, continue a source along G3BJ, produce an integral marking, or decide
`beta_C`.

## Reproduction

```powershell
python build_ust_g3cb_b69_b103_h20_frame_intertwiner.py
python verify_ust_g3cb_b69_b103_h20_frame_intertwiner.py
```

The packet is
`state/ust_g3cb_b69_b103_h20_frame_intertwiner.packet.json`; the matrix,
inverse, complete coordinate solve and 33-for-33 monomial replacement ledger
